  "id": "infantile-amnesia",
  "term": "infantile amnesia",
  "definition": "Infantile amnesia is the developmental loss from conscious access of autobiographical memories for events experienced before about ages 3 to 4. In this context, it is linked to the emergence of memory-related metacognitive and language abilities that support remembering and reporting past personal events.",
